==== Uboot web interface ====
  * Connect your computer to the *lan* port of the router.
  * See the GL.iNet website for details for getting into Uboot.
  * Alternatively, if you have a serial cable, you can type "gl" during the 2 sec pause in the boot to enter the bootloader, then type "httpd" to start the web interface.
  * Set your computer's IP address to 192.168.1.2.  You might also have manually set the default route or gateway.
  * Upload the factory firmware for *Uboot*

